&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Cision, we believe in empowering every individual to make an impact. Here, your voice is heard, your ideas are valued, and your unique perspective fuels our collective success. As part of our global team, you&#39;ll thrive in an environment that champions curiosity, collaboration, and innovation, all while making meaningful contributions to the brands we accelerate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join us in shaping the future of communication and building authentic connections that matter. Whether you&#39;re solving complex problems or driving bold innovations, your growth is our success, and together, we’ll create the conversations of tomorrow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empower your impact at Cision. Be seen, be understood, be you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Research Analyst&lt;/strong&gt;, you will support communications measurement and analytics for one of our major automotive clients, with a strong focus on &lt;strong&gt;Motorsports and Formula 1&lt;/strong&gt;. You will play a key role across reporting and data analysis, from managing media content collection and coding to analysing, synthesising and presenting insights from large and complex data sets to support business decisions.&lt;/span&

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Lightcast we are enabling scientists to gain a deeper understanding of human health and disease at the cellular level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our technology enables the direct, precise interrogation of single cell heterogeneity, interactions and functional behaviours with a level of flexibility and scale that was previously inaccessible. Across a broad range of disciplines from basic and translational research to drug discovery, we provide the freedom to accelerate discovery and apply novel biological insights.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At Lightcast we are enabling scientists to gain a deeper understanding of human health and disease at the cellular level. Our technology enables the direct, precise interrogation of single cell heterogeneity, interactions and functional behaviours with a level of flexibility and scale that was previously inaccessible. Across a broad range of disciplines from basic and translational research to drug discovery, we provide the freedom to accelerate discovery and apply novel biological insights.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Lightcast platform is a benchtop laboratory instrument that uses microfluidics to allow precise and highly flexible control of thousands of aqueous microdroplets using software-generated light patterns. Control systems enable the integrated optical, mechanical, and fluidic sub-systems to perform complex workflows and assays used in the search for drug candidates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are seeking a Senior Mechatronics Engineer to join our team and take a leading role in system design and engineering activities. The ideal candidate

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Architect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Permanent | Hybrid | North West, Frimley, Yeovil or Filton | Cloud, Infrastructure &amp;amp; Enterprise Architecture | SC cleared&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Solution Architect, you will be responsible for defining, governing and assuring end-to-end technology solutions that support both business and programme objectives. Working closely with programme teams, engineering functions, suppliers and senior stakeholders, you will ensure solutions are secure, scalable, supportable and aligned to architectural standards and strategic roadmaps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a broad, multi-disciplinary architecture background, with the ability to work across multiple technology domains rather than specialising in a single area. You&#39;ll provide architectural leadership across cloud, infrastructure, workplace technologies, networking and security, helping to shape both current delivery and future technology direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report to the System Design Authority and support architectural governance activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define solution architectures and technical designs that meet business requirements within agreed cost, time and technical constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and evolution of technology standards, strategies and roadmaps across workplace and enterprise technology portfolios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership and architectural guidance to programme and engineering teams throughout the project lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with internal and external technology suppliers, ensuring technical governance and delivery expectations are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure security principles are embedded into solution designs and support ongoing security improvement and remediation activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information Architect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Permanent | Hybrid | Data Architecture | Enterprise Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Information Data Architect&lt;/strong&gt; to design, develop and evolve information architecture across complex enterprise environments. This role will play a key part in shaping data models, improving architecture design and ensuring information solutions align with wider business and enterprise architecture strategies. Working closely with stakeholders, architects and technical teams, you will influence critical design decisions and drive improvements in how information is structured, governed and utilised across the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join a data-driven environment where information is recognised as a strategic asset. Working with advanced data platforms, business systems and enterprise architecture tools, you will support the development of robust data foundations that enable smarter decision-making and long-term organisational success. This is an excellent opportunity to contribute to enterprise-wide data and information architecture whilst helping shape future data strategy and standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain conceptual, logical and physical data models across multiple business domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with enterprise architects, technical teams and business stakeholders to ensure data solutions meet strategic, technical and operational requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support data integration initiatives and information flows, ensuring consistency, quality and interoperability across systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and apply data architecture standards, frameworks and best practices across the organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt

